{"id":"cankerworm","name":"Cankerworm","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:cankerworm"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Cankerworm","text":"(Heb. yelek), “the licking locust,” which licks up the grass of the field; probably the locust at a certain stage of its growth, just as it emerges from the caterpillar state (Joel 1:4; 2:25). The word is rendered “caterpillar” in Ps. 105:34; Jer. 51:14, 17 (but R.V. “canker-worm”). “It spoileth and fleeth away” (Nah. 3:16), or as some read the passage, “The cankerworm putteth off [i.e., the envelope of its wings], and fleeth away.”"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3218","lemma":"יֶלֶק","xlit":"yeleq","gloss":"a devourer","kjv":"cankerworm, caterpillar","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H697","lemma":"אַרְבֶּה","xlit":"ʼarbeh","gloss":"a locust","kjv":"grasshopper, locust","count":3,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H1501","lemma":"גָּזָם","xlit":"gâzâm","gloss":"a kind of locust","kjv":"palmer-worm","count":2,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H2625","lemma":"חָסִיל","xlit":"châçîyl","gloss":"the ravager","kjv":"caterpillar","count":2,"share":0.5}],"verses":["Joel.1.4","Joel.2.25","Nah.3.15","Nah.3.16"],"related":[{"id":"insects","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.07,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"locust","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.048,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"caterpillar","type":"lexical","strong":"H697","why":"both lead with אַרְבֶּה (H697)"},{"id":"insects","type":"lexical","strong":"H697","why":"both lead with אַרְבֶּה (H697)"},{"id":"locust","type":"lexical","strong":"H697","why":"both lead with אַרְבֶּה (H697)"}],"works":[]}
